# Workflow title

State the personalized outcome and the invariant that makes this workflow worth
repeating. Keep this file focused on orchestration; leave atomic procedures in
their owning skills.

## Dependencies

| Skill | Source | Requirement | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `$skill-name` | Repository, installed skill, or plugin | required | State the capability consumed by this workflow. |

## Defaults

- Record only personalized defaults that materially reduce repeated decisions.
- Allow an explicit request to override these defaults for the current run.

## Workflow

1. Preflight the declared dependencies and resolve the user's inputs.
2. Invoke each skill by identifier and pass verified outputs to the next step.
3. Keep orchestration decisions here and atomic implementation details in the
   dependency skills.

## Approval gates

- List every action that requires explicit approval, including any proposed
  substitution for an unavailable required skill.

## Completion criteria

- Define observable conditions that must all be true before reporting success.

## Failure handling

- State how to clean up partial work and report blockers.
- Explain when an optional dependency may be skipped.
- Never use a substitute for an unavailable required skill without explicit
  user approval.
